Summary: Rewrite binds to 127.x.x.x addresses macOS refuses, for GOG Galaxy
Category: system
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 24472
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Files: server/sock.c
  Changes: verbatim (CX 25.1.1 has the same code)
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: wineserver: 'HACK: rewriting bind
    loopback address to 127.0.0.1'
Upstream: no
Why: On Windows (and Linux) every 127.x.x.x address is local; macOS only
 lets a socket bind to 127.0.0.1, so a bind to another loopback address
 fails with WSAEADDRNOTAVAIL. wineserver now binds such sockets to
 127.0.0.1, so GOG Galaxy can start. getsockname still reports the address
 asked for.
Programs: GOG Galaxy: doesn't start, as macOS refuses binds to 127.x.x.x
 addresses other than 127.0.0.1
Seen on: macOS 26.7.2 (M1 Max): native binds to 127.0.0.2 and 127.1.2.3
 fail with EADDRNOTAVAIL; lo0 has only 127.0.0.1
Messages: "HACK: rewriting bind loopback address to 127.0.0.1" (wineserver's
 stderr, for each such bind; WINEDEBUG doesn't hide it)
Risk: always on: every program's binds to 127.x.x.x go to 127.0.0.1 instead;
 still loopback only, nothing is exposed off the machine
Known issues: CodeWeavers call it an incomplete and incorrect rewrite. Two
 sockets bound to different 127.x addresses on one port now collide
 (WSAEADDRINUSE; measured in Wine 11.22: 127.0.0.2, then 127.0.0.3 and
 127.0.0.1 on the same port). A connect to 127.x.x.x other than 127.0.0.1
 still fails (it times out on macOS), so a program that connects to the
 address it bound to waits for a TCP timeout.
Uncertain: which GOG Galaxy version needed it, and whether current ones
 still do.
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-25: binds to 127.0.0.2 succeed in
 macfixes-11.22-quick20261125T052251 (getsockname reports 127.0.0.2)

diff --git a/server/sock.c b/server/sock.c
index 93505d5..360fe02 100644
--- a/server/sock.c
+++ b/server/sock.c
@@ -3051,6 +3051,18 @@ static void sock_ioctl( struct fd *fd, ioctl_code_t code, struct async *async )
 
         if (unix_addr.addr.sa_family == AF_INET)
         {
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+            /* CW Hack 24472. macOS does not support binding to any loopback
+             * address other than 127.0.0.1. This is an incomplete and incorrect
+             * rewrite, but it's enough to satisfy GOG Galaxy. */
+            if ((unix_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr & 0xff) == 127 &&
+                unix_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr != htonl( INADDR_LOOPBACK ))
+            {
+                fprintf(stderr, "HACK: rewriting bind loopback address to 127.0.0.1\n");
+                bind_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl( INADDR_LOOPBACK );
+            }
+#endif
+
             if (!memcmp( &unix_addr.in.sin_addr, magic_loopback_addr, 4 )
                     || bind_to_interface( sock, &unix_addr.in ))
                 bind_addr.in.sin_addr.s_addr = htonl( INADDR_ANY );
